rocket league right now is in is in its  second PlayStation 4 beta the first beta  it was very successful and so today  we're going to show you what is in the  new beta along with some extra cool  stuff for the game spot audience that  will be in the final version but it's  not yet available in the beta one of the  things that we really like about rocket  League and working on is that we're  trying to approach it like it's a chess  type game so that on the surface it  seems like it's just cars playing soccer  and your goal is to hit the ball into  the opposite colored goal of your own  car but in reality what we're hoping  that people discover as they play is  that it's all about layers so while at  first you may just be hitting the balls  into the goals soon you realize that you  can also jump or double jump and if you  master the controls well enough you can  actually start to fly through the air  and you can do bicycle kicks and front  kicks and sidekicks you can do all sorts  of flips you can drive along the sides  of the walls and on the ceiling you can  be aggressive or defensive and all of  these elements taking together adds a  lot of strategy and a lot of competition  to what seems like a simple game but  actually is a quite complex despite it's  easy to play nature the game is  completely physics-based so where you go  and how you go is completely based on  how fast you're going and the angles  that you take things we wanted to make  sure that the game felt balanced so that  whenever you're playing that the cars do  what you expect them to do and that  you're not surprised by what happens  that you feel in control at all times  and one of the keys to doing that is  understanding your boost meter which is  in the the lower right-hand corner there  you can increase that by going over  those little lighted circles that you  see on the field and as that goes up  that gives you more boost eventually you  can actually go supersonic speeds if you  have enough of it and hold it down long  enough but allows you to do some really  cool goals  we also have a new item called season  mode which we're going to talk about  closer to release later the summer which  we're still working on but the season  mode is going to be we think a lot of  fun it's going to be much closer to  traditional season modes we find that  something like a madman or a fifa where  you can create your own team take them  through an entire season against other  teams you can customize what your team  looks your opponents will some will be  harder some will be easier you'll play  in all sorts of different stadiums we we  think that it's going to add a lot of  layers for players who before have only  ever thought of the game as a  multiplayer only game but we also wanted  to make sure that this time around we  have a lot of single-player options one  of the things that is not available in  the beta that we came here specifically  to show is the the ability to customize  your car in the garage so in the garage  mode in the final game you can see that  we have multiple car types will have at  least ten at launch and each one is this  is a very specific thing now is that  there are no stats or abilities  assigning these cars we wanted to keep  the game as balanced as possible and as  fair as possible so there are only real  differences in these cars besides their  look is where their hit boxes are  located so that's the slight alteration  that you'll see in how they play  otherwise we wanted to make sure that  it's all about personal customization  and expression and in the original game  all you could do was change your skin  here you can see now that we allow you  to change your paint color for both  primary and your accent color we also  have various paint types so we're still  working on how many we're going to have  in the finished version so don't  necessarily read too much into how many  appear on our list here but if you were  to select wood or glossy for example  those are different paint types we also  plan to include matt semi-gloss metallic  things like that the old up players  really customize the way that their  their car looks in a much more  interesting way than we had before we  also have new tires we have you can  update your rocket boost we have toppers  which are essentially  and that means that we have everything  from the mariachi hat which is a  favorite to the police the police cherry  top two other we have other all sorts of  facility we have silly things like a  traditional sombrero we have a whole  bunch of things that we don't want to  spoil the surprise on that are really  funny we also have things like taxi  toppers and pizza delivery toppers all  sorts of different things that will make  people feel like the cars their own and  antennas are also another good example  we have a ton of different countries in  there you can unlock other other flags  that are either funny or silly or look  really cool camouflage Flags traffic  flags team flags from our season mode  all sorts of things all in all we're  looking at more than a hundred and fifty  different items that you can customize  your car with at launch and we plan on  adding more things post launch as well  and one of the keys that we think to  keeping people involved is there's no  super complicated way and how these  unlock every time you play a game soon  as you're done you will unlock a new  item we didn't want to we wanted to make  sure that people were always looking  forward to the next thing and so we  think that as long as we're rewarding  them for playing the game that will keep  them interested and that's rocket League  we hope you liked what you saw we have a  lot more to show you as we get closer to  release later this summer exclusively on  playstation 4 4 consoles and also on PC  later in the year we really hope that  you have fun when you play the beta and  we'll see you there  you
 

